  "result": "Perfect! All 256 tests pass. The overdue invoices report feature is complete:\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **src/reports.js** \u2014 New module with helper functions and report:\n   - `balanceDue(invoice)` \u2014 Calculates unpaid amount on invoice\n   - `daysOverdue(dueDate, asOf)` \u2014 Calculates days between due date and report date\n   - `overdueInvoices(invoices, asOf)` \u2014 Generates overdue report\n     - Filters for status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' only\n     - Filters for dueDate strictly before asOf\n     - Returns array of `{ number, customerId, dueDate, daysOverdue, due }`\n     - Sorted by daysOverdue descending (most overdue first)\n\n2. **Test coverage** \u2014 18 comprehensive tests verifying:\n   - Empty invoice handling\n   - Draft invoice exclusion\n   - Overdue invoice inclusion\n   - Not-yet-due invoice exclusion\n   - Days overdue calculation (1, 9, 250+ days)\n   - Due amount from invoiceTotals\n   - Due amount after partial payment\n   - Paid invoice exclusion\n   - Partially paid invoice inclusion\n   - Sorting by daysOverdue (descending)\n   - Single day overdue edge case\n   - Zero days overdue exclusion (not due yet)\n   - Multiple customers\n   - Different terms (NET14, EOM)\n   - Large time gaps\n   - Future invoices exclusion\n   - Invoice number preservation\n   - Discount interactions\n\n**Total: 256 tests passing** (238 + 18 new)",
